["amend","DOCS-S5-T1",1780772928,"5207ee28-cdd8-48e6-98dc-7da179d4a40d",{"scope":["cmd/armature/install_skills.go","cmd/armature/install_skills_test.go","internal/skillsembed/plugin.json (new)"],"acceptance":["After arm install-skills, .claude/plugins/armature/plugin.json exists","Skill tool can invoke armature-coordinator by name without error","All four role skills appear in system-reminder available-skills list","make check green"],"definition_of_done":"arm install-skills deploys role skills as a proper Claude Code plugin (under .claude/plugins/armature/ with plugin.json) so they appear in the model system-reminder and are invocable via Skill tool. .claude/skills/ deployment retained for slash-command access. All four role skills load via Skill tool after install."}]
["note","DOCS-S5-T1",1780772940,"5207ee28-cdd8-48e6-98dc-7da179d4a40d",{"msg":"Root cause confirmed 2026-06-06: .claude/skills/ creates skill-dir commands (slash commands for humans) in a separate registry from plugin skills. Skill tool only searches the plugin registry. Debug: 'getSkills returning: 22 skill dir commands, 32 plugin skills' — disjoint sets. Writing flat .md files to .claude/skills/ does NOT fix this. Fix: arm install-skills must also write .claude/plugins/armature/ with plugin.json so Claude Code registers skills in the plugin registry. Reference the superpowers plugin at ~/.claude/plugins/ for the correct structure.","note_id":"note-1780772940488426842"}]
